Okay, so its super common for people to be very FORWARD about where they have worked BEFORE in their linked in bios, etc. now. As if your past places are as important as your present. "Previously at Apple, Facebook, whatever..."

But, I now see this even more with young people, who maybe were just interns there for like 6 weeks. Are you really "previously at" a place if you just interned there for the summer? Isn't that a bit extreme? why does this bother me so much.